---
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
---

<div class="property-section">
  <Code
    code={`"populate": {
                "directories": [""],
                "fileType": "",
                "fullFileAndPath": false,
                "order": "date",
                "labelWhenEmpty": "No Files",
                "defaultLabel": ""
            }`}
    lang="json"
  />
  <p>
    Sets the type of file to search for, and the directories to look in. You can specify multiple file types by using
    the following pattern <code>*.txt;*.csv;*.dat</code>. If no directories are specified, the file browser will try to
    access the current working directory. Note it's always best to set the <code>directories</code> property from your
    Csound code in order to make sure the path is correct. For example, the following code will set the directory to
    that of the current .csd file.
  </p>
  <Code code={`cabbageSet "presetCombo", "populate.directory", chnget:S("CSD_PATH")`} lang="csound" />
  <p>
    The items can be ordered by "date", "size" or "alphabetically". "defaultLabel" sets the initial text when the
    combobox first appears. If it's empty, the first item on the list will appear by default.
  </p>
</div>
